    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it’s not really about specific moments. it’s just that the view from the edge... it feels so much more honest than the path. the path was just constant struggle. but out here, looking down into that quiet, it feels like there's a certain kind of grace in just letting go of the climb. like, isn't there something peaceful about finally reaching the end of a long road?",
